tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagua\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>see, that only tells me what a &quot;bagua&quot; means- not a bagua user. I understand that it is a symbol, but what is the &quot;user&quot; thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T16:17:31-07:00","id":702594,"title":"","content":"If there isn't some kind of Victorian group that has limped along for a century before being stranded by the handover of Hong Kong, I quit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=702436#post702436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW guys. Don't forget that a lot Manchurian Canditate like ideas are covered in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/344770-repost-revild-s-hotel-mascaron\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hotel-mascaron</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I still think this is the beat fan-made material I've seen for the nWoD so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T18:08:55-07:00","id":702761,"title":"","content":"I'd say you want to build this Conspiracy from the ground up, not the top down. Why is it Chinese? If that's our main focus let's look at what the Vigil might be like in the People's Republic. I'd also suggest deciding early on if you want it to be more technology-flavored, magic-flavored, or somewhere in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T18:17:15-07:00","id":702765,"title":"","content":"If you want to see a real life example of Chinese secret societies that have a mystical bent to them look up the history of the triads and the tongs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T19:49:36-07:00","id":702942,"title":"","content":"I was attempting to write a Conspiracy that hunted down Sin-Eaters as a way to atone for their ancestors in Diyu, the Chinese equivalent of Hell. Of course, after reading a bit of the Book of the Dead and finding the section for Lowgate Prison, I felt it to be too conflicting to make sense. It kinda petered out after the first few paragraphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T20:50:18-07:00","id":702970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=702594#post702594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there isn't some kind of Victorian group that has limped along for a century before being stranded by the handover of Hong Kong, I quit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ashwood Abbey's been around since the first book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T00:25:09-07:00","id":703070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy#post701969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">China is big. China is powerful. China is a strong country, and is likely to be outside of VALKYRIE's reach. In sort, China deserves its own governmental conspiracy</div> </div> </div> </div> Valkyrie is a UN task force, China is a charter member of the UN, so yes Valkyrie can have a presence in China.<br /> <br /> Now how much of a presence and how much cooperation they actually get is another matter. <br /> <br /> As for original ideas, how about an anti-ghost/sin-eater conspiracy that can trace its origins to the Boxer Rebellion?<br /> <br /> The boxers thought they were possessed by ghosts who would make them bullet proof, among other things.<br /> <br /> Well, of course they could have just been delusional, but this is the world of darkness perhaps the Boxer Rebellion would have gone a lot farther if not for the actions of a band of exorcists.<br /> <br /> As for what kind of techniques they could have to call their own- Ghost tech? Ectoplasm based alchemy? Religious rituals? Yang based martial arts techniques?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T01:36:40-07:00","id":703098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Valkyrie is a UN task force, </div> </div> </div>Isn't it a NATO taskforce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T02:37:21-07:00","id":703127,"title":"","content":"It is NATO according to Compacts and Conspiracies, and before that it felt a lot more like an American Task Force. I don't recall any mention of it as a UN Task Force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T05:21:15-07:00","id":703232,"title":"","content":"Oh well, remembered that wrong, the perils of posting while really really tired. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If no one liked my idea about exorcists formed in response to the boxer rebellion, how about geomancers?<br /> <br /> Geomancy is versatile enough you could make their primary enemies any number of the splats.<br /> <br /> If they manipulate spiritual resonance, they'll deal with spirits, and by extension werewolves.<br /> <br /> Manipulating probability would probably come to the attention of mages or possibly demons (the god machine probably wouldn't appreciate its plans getting screwed up because a mortal is messing with probability).<br /> <br /> They might form ley lines and mess with the resonance of tass and mana, which would probably get them attention of mages.<br /> <br /> The concept of chi reminds me of mummy sekhem, so to mummies geomancers might be sorcerers they have no love for. <br /> <br /> Heck, messing with the nature of a beast's lair might be possible, like say making the area it's based on calm or serene. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T05:52:03-07:00","id":703248,"title":"","content":"hey- all ideas are valid and interesting in this thread, IMO <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The problem is, however, making a full writeup to one (or more, but that is just the optimistic me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:07:22-07:00","id":703298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=703232#post703232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If no one liked my idea about exorcists formed in response to the boxer rebellion, how about geomancers?<br /> <br /> Geomancy is versatile enough you could make their primary enemies any number of the splats.<br /> <br /> If they manipulate spiritual resonance, they'll deal with spirits, and by extension werewolves.<br /> <br /> Manipulating probability would probably come to the attention of mages or possibly demons (the god machine probably wouldn't appreciate its plans getting screwed up because a mortal is messing with probability).<br /> <br /> They might form ley lines and mess with the resonance of tass and mana, which would probably get them attention of mages.<br /> <br /> The concept of chi reminds me of mummy sekhem, so to mummies geomancers might be sorcerers they have no love for.<br /> <br /> Heck, messing with the nature of a beast's lair might be possible, like say making the area it's based on calm or serene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the pattern for supplements is three compacts and a conspiracy. And Exorcism is a Tactic already. So...<br /> <br /> Your exorcist group as a compact with a minor Endowment that makes them better at using the Exorcism Tactic.<br /> <br /> Nofather's tong, with their Black Lotus, giving them a sort of hyperawareness that lets them see supernatural creatures for what they are (again, a minor endowment).<br /> <br /> My government conspiracy (in fluff terms, but a compact in game terms), with a talent for brainwashing, but a super-mundane one rather than a full on AA-social analogue).<br /> <br /> Your geomancers with a large-scale Endowment allowing cleansing of areas, manipulation of luck and resonance, detection of other influences, making it easier or harder for spirits to manifest, and so on.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T14:27:57-07:00","id":703819,"title":"","content":"actually, I think they are going to break away from that pattern- Edo's Dark Era has 4 compacts and 2 conspiracies, while I believe that Beast's Mortal Remains chapter is going to have 5 groups. Not that I'm saying that the pattern doesn't work, just that if there is a good idea, we shouldn't stop from developing it because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T04:18:06-07:00","id":704661,"title":"","content":"Yes, with a population of over 1 billion and a history that extends farther than 3000 years, I'd say there's room for as many groups as one wanted to come with. <br /> <br /> Any historical (as in would be no longer around in a modern day game) ideas swimming in anyone's head?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T00:24:30-07:00","id":708314,"title":"","content":"Hmm. <br /> <br /> We've had Valkyrie for a military organization, and VASCU for traditional police so...<br /> <br /> Time for a secret police force that also has economic components!<br /> <br /> <b>Unit Huo (Better name pending) </b><br /> <br /> Formed during the Cultural Revolution, the unit has one over arching goal: the protection of the Chinese people, and its culture, from supernatural influence. The two weapons in its arsenal are economic and flame based violence. The financial, and other economic assets, of an opponent are seized either through purchasing them out from under them, such as stock market manipulation causing a target to be stripped of corporations which provide it with money, or more covert means, such as kidnapping key personnel to the functioning of a corporation. This tool not only weakens a target through denying them financial resources, but frequently can enrich China proper through providing it an economic advantage. <br /> <br /> When supernatural entities are present in China proper, they will be dealt with through shock and awe tactics, backed by quite literal flame. Frequently, the unit will launch an attack with flash bangs, and then burst into the target's location with flamethrowers. This particular weapon came out of finding targets that were both resistant to bullets, but also especially vulnerable to fire. Additionally, many of the unit's actions can be disguised as either acts of arson by unwanted parts of society, or even as accidental fires. <br /> <br /> Okay, so the above very possibly sucked, but hey, a starting point perhaps. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T17:56:34-07:00","id":709631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=708314#post708314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> ....Okay, so the above very possibly sucked...</div> </div> </div> </div>Three people including myself disagree. Pyromania is quite nice for most threats. And Secret Police can be a nice concept in of itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...Though I'll admit with an option of a Chinese Conspiracy, a significant portion of me really would like something Wuxia flavored... Perhaps not the crazy mountain men who are basically wizards with epic kungfu, but you get the point...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T19:31:57-07:00","id":709807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=709631#post709631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three people including myself disagree. Pyromania is quite nice for most threats. And Secret Police can be a nice concept in of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> But okay, going to expand on this a tad, like maybe figure out some sort of Endowment soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:41:17-07:00","id":711366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Formed during the Cultural Revolution, </div> </div> </div>I don't think that makes sense (you could make it fit, but it'd need more explanation). I'd choose a later period. The Cultural Revolution was basically the implosion of the PRC state. No one is going to setting up secret police units.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:55:55-07:00","id":711377,"title":"","content":"<b>Unit Huo's Recruitment and Equipment</b><br /> <br /> There are two groups of recruits for Unit Huo, one for the organization's economic components, the other for its brute force operations. The first group are a mix of hackers, bankers, and business graduates to manipulate as many separate aspects of an opponent's financial assets as possible. They are primarily motivated by a single promise, they will gain a share of the riches that any operation entails. Stock shares in valuable companies, the possibility of eliminating costly competition, or just traditional cash. On the flip side, the group understands that any significant transgression shall result in their deaths, and their accounts being shared amongst the rest of the group. <br /> <br /> The second group is recruited from a mixture of ideological zealots and brainwashed former dissidents. As China has evolved as a society, brainwashing has become the dominant method of recruitment from less zealots to go around, and for the unit's operations becoming much more economic in nature. Regardless, the training necessary has stayed relatively the same. <br /> <br /> Units are trained to move as quickly as possible once flash bangs, tear gas, or similar disruptive grenades have been deployed. Flamethrowers are used to incinerate any enemy forces, the structures they live in, and any objects they may have regularly interacted with. Training has them carry out the entire process in the space of minutes, only having to slow down to insure everything has been doused in flame. The need to incinerate even the objects of the supernatural comes from a mixture of fearing curses, and political considerations, as many supernatural entities happen to be political dissidents, or otherwise threaten the state. Therefore, propaganda pamphlets and the like were to be incinerated, so as to prevent their spread. <br /> <br /> As armor, and also to conceal their identities, Unit Huo wear full body fire retardant clothing, and gas masks. These suits also come with technology that protects against much more esoteric threats, such as something that cancels out the voice of anyone except the commander of the unit. This consideration arose from an incident involving cults during the Cultural Revolution, and once again, political considerations to protect the unit from foreign ideas unnecessary to their current mission. <br /> <br /> The most important aspect of their training however is what makes them truly terrifying as hunters. Regardless of their source, recruits are sent through a gauntlet of fears, ranging from total darkness, being covered in insects, and most of all, fire. By the end, the militant section of Unit Huo will be almost immune to fear based paralysis. Those in the unit are still capable of feeling fear, it was found units without the emotion at all were quite useless, but are able to control it on a level that most human beings are not. Even effects known to occur in the presence of Werewolves can be resisted, although not completely ignored. <br /> <br /> (Possibly of OP ability, but, fits the theme, so, tell me guys what you think regardless.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:58:56-07:00","id":711506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As China has evolved as a society, brainwashing has become the dominant method of recruitment from less zealots to go around, </div> </div> </div>Why? I mean, the organisation has a pretty benign purpose. Plenty of Chinese people are probably on board with the mission to protect China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T18:00:47-07:00","id":711508,"title":"","content":"Task Force Valkyrie is an American organization. Sometimes it will invite persons from countries which are allied to the USA, but it serves American interests only. At least it's what the books say, if I'm not wrong.if","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/8.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","name":"Kergonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T18:34:12-07:00","id":711544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=711506#post711506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? I mean, the organisation has a pretty benign purpose. Plenty of Chinese people are probably on board with the mission to protect China.</div> </div> </div> </div>A... excellent point. <br /> <br /> My only counter is the organization going for the ideological fanatic theme, as... well, there's a reason its born out of the Cultural Revolution. Well, that, and the economic stuff I don't think is that benign. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure a ton of people would be down with the brutal anti-fear therapy. It could be the government decides the dissidents are disposable enough to justify having parts of their personality destroyed basically. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T19:36:08-07:00","id":711636,"title":"","content":"<b>Unit Huo's History</b><br /> <br /> When Mao began a purge of China in the so called, &quot;Cultural Revolution,&quot; the purge would accidentally run into supernatural entities. Many cultural and religious sites contained supernatural entities that would violently defend them. Additionally, many persons were found to be supernatural entities in the process of defending themselves from Red Guard units. The response to these incidents didn't come from on high, but from the same people carrying out the purge to begin with, the Red Guard. <br /> <br /> Armed with little more than ideological zeal, the Red Guard formed a unit in secret to combat the supernatural. They sought to cleanse the country of Vampires, Werewolves, Witches, and who knows what else for the same reason the Cultural Revolution was conducted. They saw them as tools of either foreigners seeking to stop the Revolution, or reactionaries seeking to drag China back to the past. This unit would end up adopting fire based weapons, initially molotov cocktails, when they found bullets did little to nothing frequently against supernatural entities, and that up close combat was a waste of time against enemies that frequently possessed far more strength than any human. <br /> <br /> The other tactic to form from this time was the idea of a fear based gauntlet to harden the unit against the effects of the supernatural. Starting with tests like being trapped in a dark room, being near predatory animals, and having to stand near flame for extended periods of time, the idea would evolve. Even in its beginnings, it would start to have impacts on how troops operated. <br /> <br /> When the Red Guard were crushed by the PLA, Unit Huo was spared. Initially, its high casualty rate was seen as a way to make the Red Guard less destructive, however, the unit became something else with time. Supernatural entities did exist, and more importantly, they were a danger to the People's Republic of China. Both its populace and culture were at threat from them, so a unit devoted to destroying them that happened to contain ideological zealots the state had no other use for was best. <br /> <br /> This official recognition would lead to the unit gaining proper flamethrowers, and its anti-fear training to be expanded drastically. Additionally, the first attempts to brainwash political dissidents to be part of the group would begin during this 2nd period in its history, as the supply of ideological zealots began to dry up. <br /> <br /> The unit would never be known to Mao himself, always hidden as a spec-ops project, or some other aspect of the military. This would pay dividends when Mao died, and the reformists took over. This period, with the introduction of economic reforms, came with it the introduction of the next aspect of the group, its economic component. Certain supernatural entities were extremely wealthy, and acquiring that wealth for China was seen as an extremely desirable goal. Additionally, it would allow the group to continue to possess revolutionary zeal without interfering with China's reform process. In later times, this component would instead act as a way for more moderate persons to join Unit Huo, and for it to give China access to extreme wealth. <br /> <br /> To this day, the unit has continued to evolve. It was found completely eliminating fear, even if possible on a mass scale, was undesirable because it lead to far less effective personnel. Body armor was added, along with gas masks, and the speed centric aspect of the Unit, by adopting tactics from police forces around the world. This change coincided with it becoming a secret police unit, and having the powers to arrest individuals suspected of working with, or supporting supernatural entities. Some of these persons would later become more personnel for Unit Huo after brainwashing was done to them. <br /> <br /> And so it continues on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T20:08:03-07:00","id":711680,"title":"","content":"So, the conspiracy isn't done yet, as it lacks a proper set of endowments, however, I'm going to lay out some thoughts for what I was going for. <br /> <br /> For one, I feel like we lack a Hunter group made up of ideological zealots. We have religious zealots with both a Conspiracy, MM, and a Compact, the Long Night. We're not even touching on groups like the Ascending Ones, which very probably have religious extremists in their service, even if they aren't themselves. By contrast, the closest thing we have to ideological extremists are ultra-nationalists(a Compact I can't remember the name of). Task Force: Valkyrie really doesn't count. <br /> <br /> Additionally, I feel like the Cultural Revolution, in all its horribleness, would be a birthplace for Hunters. Violently purging China's past I feel like would inevitably run into supernatural entities or things, and such would provoke a response. <br /> <br /> Hence, the fanatic aspect of Unit Huo. <br /> <br /> The economic part I was going for is that we've had corporations seeking to use the supernatural for profit obviously, but governments? The Chinese government in real life does a lot of actions devoted to increasing the wealth of either its party members or the country proper, and it feels logical to me a hunter group would continue that. That they could target say, filthy rich Vampires that have built up their wealth over the centuries, means there are plenty of targets for such. Unlike say, the Cheiron Group, they could literally seize the financial assets of such entities, with many interesting implications for play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:20:13-07:00","id":712630,"title":"","content":"<b>Unit Huo's Enemy</b> <br /> <br /> Unit Huo has one primary opponent they seek out above all others: Cults. During the Cultural Revolution, one of the primary sources of supernatural opponents were cults worshipping supernatural entities in the rural parts of China, or violently protecting religious sites. That these cults are almost automatically political dissidents means they are an opponent Unit Huo seeks to completely wipe out from China proper, and even when conducting foreign operations, they seek to disrupt Cults whenever they run across them. <br /> <br /> Outside of that, the specialty is in supernatural entities that possess great wealth. This continues to be justified as targeting the international bourgeois, which is true from the perspective of robbing supernatural entities of the ability to manipulate or control China with their immense wealth. Additionally, the wealth gained from these endeavors not only helps fund Unit Huo, but also enrich China itself. This focus is the one aspect of Unit Huo that intentionally engages in international operations, and has gotten to the point that the unit has an income in the hundreds of millions of dollars per year in seized financial assets alone. Dozens of corporations are seized, through killing supernatural entities, stock market manipulation, and intimidating the rest of the company's board into accepting ownership by Chinese persons. <br /> <br /> This economic focus makes the unit extremely controversial within the Hunter community, but also insures it always gets good funding from the Chinese government. After all, it is a net gain in regards to income, and has also gained China valuable technology through their seizures of economic assets. <br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes </b><br /> <br /> <b>Union: </b>&quot;Some of them are potential brothers and sisters in our struggle. Otherwise, they lack the tools we do to carry out the revolution.&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night: </b>&quot;You pray to your God, but where is he when your children are killed before your eyes, or when your crosses are simply laughed at?&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>Task Force VALKYRIE: </b>&quot;They claim to serve their country, but they do not enrich it, nor do they attack those who rob it most. What sort of patriot allows the ill gotten fortunes of supernatural enemies to be uncontested?&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>Cherion Group: </b>&quot;The true way to profit off of monsters is to rob their assets, not just their bodies. When you've long finished profiting off their corpses, we still enjoy the many benefits of their corporations.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T19:09:37-07:00","id":716833,"title":"","content":"<b>Unit Huo's Endowments</b><br /> <br /> Alright, guys, I really need your help on this one. Specifically, you need to see if, <br /> <br /> A. The Endowments aren't hilariously overpowered, <br /> <br /> B. They aren't far too weak to matter. <br /> <br /> <b>Strength of the Driven </b><br /> <br /> The primary tool of Unit Huo is their powerful training. Rather than using magic, or cutting edge technology, although they certainly have technology available, they rely on special training. Everything from fearsome speed, resisting supernatural abilities, and much stranger abilities are possible from their unique training. <br /> <br /> <b>Anti-Fearing Therapy (1-3 dots) </b><br /> <br /> Constant exposure to intense fear, such as predatory animals or certain types of torture, teaches a recruit to control their fear. In the field, any supernatural ability that causes paralysis, running away, or other impacts, through overwhelming fear of the entity automatically loses one to three successes against the agent.<br /> <br /> <b>Rapid Movement (2 dots)</b><br /> <br /> Agents are taught to move as quickly as possible, and fight as rapidly as their equipment allows. Once completed, an agent can outpace the ability of an opponent to respond to them. Add two dice to gaining initiative, and two dice to defense to reflect this training. <br /> <br /> <b>Higher Loyalty (1-5 dots)</b><br /> <br /> A Hunter of Unit Huo should be loyal to the People and the Revolution, above all else. This is reinforced through constant propaganda, and intense brainwashing. Each dot removes a success from any roll to mind control an agent, regardless of means. <br /> <br /> What I have for now. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T03:40:48-07:00","id":718470,"title":"","content":"well, in order to decide the power level of the Unit's Endowments, you first need to decide how one acquires them- I understand that each power is bought separately, but does there any limitation about the number of powers you may have? Is there a cost you need to pay for gaining/using them? Can you strength them or weaken them somehow? Things like that. Also, deciding on the way you get those powers is a good way to reinforce the identity of the group.<br /> <br /> And on a general, I really like that group. They are very interesting, and I really want to see how they may work with other Chinese/ East Asian organizations.<br /> <br /> Also- do you have any idea about the Status benefits the Unite gains?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 10-23-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T11:19:28-07:00","id":719940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/701969-lets-make-a-chinese-conspiracy?p=718470#post718470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, in order to decide the power level of the Unit's Endowments, you first need to decide how one acquires them- I understand that each power is bought separately, but does there any limitation about the number of powers you may have? Is there a cost you need to pay for gaining/using them? Can you strength them or weaken them somehow? Things like that. Also, deciding on the way you get those powers is a good way to reinforce the identity of the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. <br /> <br /> Right now, they arise from special training, and I'm not sure what, if any, limitations there'd be on how many you could have. After all, they're special training, so the limitation is the experience, and time perhaps, a character would be willing to devote to acquiring said training. <br /> <br /> Their might be a split depending on whether you're in the economic or brute force portion of Unit Huo. After all, it doesn't really make sense for say, the hackers of the group to have anti-fear therapy, because they aren't supposed to be on the front lines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on a general, I really like that group. They are very interesting, and I really want to see how they may work with other Chinese/ East Asian organizations. </div> </div> </div>Great!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also- do you have any idea about the Status benefits the Unite gains? </div> </div> </div>I think they'd have some sort of benefit from being secret police, and being a source of income for China. Tricky bit is they need to have status benefits that apply relatively equal to two very different parts. So, coming soon!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:07:18-07:00","id":720089,"title":"","content":"<b>Unit Huo Status Benefits and Factions</b><br /> <br /> Unit Huo is a strange conspiracy in that it has two parts that are radically different from each other, and that barely ever crossover. Their recruitment is different, as one seeks to attain great wealth for China, while another seeks the destruction of its enemies. Additionally, the Conspiracy bears the marks of China's turbulent history, and the fires of its origins. <br /> <br /> <b>Sections<br /> <br /> The Red Section</b>: The original group, and the one that most bears the marks of its origins in the Cultural Revolution. Focusing mostly on destroying those who corrupt China from within, they still possess the ideological zeal, whether from brainwashing or being zealots themselves, that motivated the Red Guard decades ago. They're the brute force section of the organization, and their zeal makes them the devoted. But what if they decide China has strayed too far from its ideals? <br /> <br /> <b>The Gold Section: </b>The newest section, and the one devoted to acquiring great wealth for China. More moderate than the Red Section, others in the organization accuse them of being little different than those they rob. Oddly enough, many within have become disillusioned with both Capitalism and Communism, for their exploits have shown them the worst parts of both. Additionally, a fiery Nationalism possesses the faction now, feeling that they're recovering the wealth stolen from China by imperialism, and later on, mistakes of its own government. Such motivation is worrisome for those who control the organization, for they may decide to use their wealth to steer China onto the same path Japan once took. <br /> <br /> <b>The White Section: </b>Administrators of the organization, they're the closest to the state, and one that authorizes operations. Their color being associated with death suits this role, for what they authorize has indeed incurred immense carnage. Increasingly, they must deal with an organization that loathes the country it serves for either lacking ideological purity, or being perceived as selling itself to foreigners. The organization cannot operate without the ideological zeal that pushes it forward, and China has become dependent on Unit Huo not only to protect it from the supernatural, but also an important source of income for China itself. The only they can do is try to push the Red and Gold Section into operations that distract them from their feelings on China itself. <br /> <br /> <b>Status Benefits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Status 1</b>: You're new, and disposable, but, you can acquire the training that sets the organization apart with merit dots. <br /> <br /> <b>Status 3: </b>You've demonstrated loyalty to the group, and enough competence to have survived this long. For this, you've gained secret police powers and can, under sufficient justification, mark anyone as a target. This will give them the Condition, &quot;Target by Unit Huo,&quot; which authorizes operates by both Red and Gold Section against them. Anyone, or anything, possessing Target by Unit Huo will be easier to find, represented by two extra dice on any roll involving Investigation in acquiring the target, or investigating their potential wealth. Failure to properly use this capability however will result in a loss of status, if not worse. <br /> <br /> <b>Status 5: </b>You don't go out on operations too often. When you do, you will have the full power of the organization to back you up. Gain four dots in Allies, representing Unit Huo, that you can call to back you up on any operation. Note, if this is abused, you can lose this status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T14:15:38-07:00","id":720572,"title":"","content":"So... the Conspiracy is finished!<br /> <br /> And judging by reception so far, its my best conspiracy yet<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm toying with creating an opposite, of sorts, but, I'm unsure where it'll arise. <br /> <br /> Besides, I'm sure somebody else has ideas for the thread.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 10-23-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T02:45:57-07:00","id":734149,"title":"","content":"All in all, I think this is a cool conspiracy. Now, with the Unit and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/713613-compact-the-red-envelope-society\">Red Envelope Society</a>, we have 2 Chinese hunter groups! Anyone has an idea how to develop other ideas from the thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:00:26-07:00","id":735587,"title":"","content":"I would suggest for whoever else wants to contribute to consider using Taiwan, as while that isn't mainland China, you could easily have a Chinese Conspiracy related to it. Additionally, this could be where a mystical themed Chinese hunter group would retreat to after the Communists take over China, opening up options that are unlikely to survive the Cultural Revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}